                  4.00  :  T H E   D E M O

   Released at the Europa Micro Systems summer party, June 1990.

   Machine .... ARM/AT, ARM926EJ-S at 100 MHz, VGA, PC speaker
   Code ....... C for the frame, hand-written ARM assembler for
                everything that touches a pixel (FX.S)
   Music ...... PC speaker, one voice, played from INT 08h with
                the 8253 at 1120 Hz (70 Hz player, arpeggio chords)

   Parts: starfield intro, plasma, rotozoomer, tunnel, copper
   bars, and a sine scroller that tells you how it was done.

   Keys: SPACE next part, ESC back to DOS.
   Options: DEMO /Q (no music)  /P n (start at part n)  /T s (quit
            after s seconds)

   Turn the Turbo off and watch the frame rate drop - it will tell
   you on exit how much of the ARM it used.

   Greetings to everybody who ever typed DEBUG and G=100.
